messages.reasoning_content:
Great! The client pod `allowed-client` has the label `role=allowed`.

Now I can patch the `default-deny-ingress` NetworkPolicy to allow ingress traffic from pods matching `role=allowed` to the server pods (`app=server`).

The patch:

```json
{
  "spec": {
    "ingress": [
      {
        "from": [
          {
            "podSelector": {
              "matchLabels": {
                "role": "allowed"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "ports": [
          {
            "protocol": "TCP",
            "port": 80
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

I will apply this patch. I will assume TCP/80 is the required protocol/port, as no specific port was given for the application server, but this is a common default for "application server" access.

